cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pen-score, please cite it using this metadata."
authors:
  - family-names: "Mahaboob Ali"
    given-names: "Anees Ahmed"
    email: ahmedaneesm@gmail.com
    affiliation: "VIT University, Vellore"
title: "PEN-SCORE: Multi-axis scoring framework for programmable genome editors"
version: 0.1.3
date-released: 2026-05-25
url: "https://github.com/ahmedanees-m/pen-score"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmedanees-m/pen-score"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  pen-score is an 8-axis computational scoring framework for ranking programmable
  genome editors by therapeutic potential. It produces a weighted composite
  PenScore from axes measuring DSB safety, off-target specificity, cargo capacity,
  AAV deliverability, immunogenicity, programmability, therapeutic maturity, and
  metabolic energy independence. Five pre-registered predictions were evaluated on
  the public scorecard (29 editors, v0.1.1); 4/4 evaluable predictions PASS.
  v0.1.3 adds the get_editor_metadata() API (EditorMetadata dataclass with
  intrinsic_cargo_mechanism and cell_based_evidence fields for PEN-COMPARE v3.2),
  canonicalises IS622 as ISCro4 (UniProt D2TGM5) with IS622 retained as a
  deprecated alias (DeprecationWarning), and raises test coverage from 68% to
  93% (267 tests). Dependency pins updated to mech-class>=0.5.4 and
  genome-atlas>=0.7.2.
keywords:
  - genome editing
  - CRISPR
  - gene therapy
  - programmable nucleases
  - recombinases
  - multi-axis scoring
  - pen-score
  - PEN-STACK
